{"name":"Hypebeast culture","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/HYPEBEAST-Logo_%282022%29.png/960px-HYPEBEAST-Logo_%282022%29.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HYPEBEAST-Logo_(2022).png","caption":"HYPEBEAST-Logo (2022)","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Hypebeast culture is a youth fashion culture centred on buying highly sought-after streetwear: limited drops, collaborations, sneakers and logo-heavy pieces from brands such as Supreme, Stussy and A Bathing Ape. For appearance, it offers a ready-made style identity built on recognisable, current pieces.","The term began in the mid-2000s, initially as a derogatory label for people who bought streetwear mainly to follow trends; Hong Kong journalist Kevin Ma took the word for his fashion blog Hypebeast. Today it is used descriptively, ironically or affectionately, depending on region."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Followers follow release calendars and drops announced on social media, buy limited items at retail or on resale markets, and build outfits around sneakers, hoodies, tees and caps with visible branding. Style media such as Hypebeast report on collaborations and releases."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Limited releases can be expensive on resale markets, and critics say reselling prioritises profit and prestige over style. Spending pressure and the quick cycling of trends are commonly noted."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/HYPEBEAST-Logo_%282022%29.png/960px-HYPEBEAST-Logo_%282022%29.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/HYPEBEAST-Logo_%282022%29.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"HYPEBEAST-Logo (2022)","license":"Public domain","creator":"Hypebeast Ltd.","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HYPEBEAST-Logo_(2022).png","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/HYPEBEAST-Logo.svg/960px-HYPEBEAST-Logo.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/HYPEBEAST-Logo.svg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"HYPEBEAST-Logo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Stellalo101medialab","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HYPEBEAST-Logo.svg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/99/Hypebeast_logo.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/99/Hypebeast_logo.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Hypebeast logo","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Stellalo101medialab","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hypebeast_logo.png","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4d/Hypebeast-Logo-512-2.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4d/Hypebeast-Logo-512-2.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Hypebeast-Logo-512-2","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Stellalo101medialab","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hypebeast-Logo-512-2.png","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Hypebeast_logo_2022.svg/960px-Hypebeast_logo_2022.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/84/Hypebeast_logo_2022.svg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Hypebeast logo 2022","license":"Public domain","creator":"Hypebeast Hong Kong Ltd.","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hypebeast_logo_2022.svg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Hypebeast.jpg/960px-Hypebeast.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ae/Hypebeast.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Hypebeast","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Silvio Aang Brüst","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hypebeast.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/1b7d366c-0153-42b4-8e42-1d6477304a42/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/3301/3330410116_f5c1d9c201_b.jpg","title":"Hypebeast Credit Crunch edition","license":"BY-NC-ND 2.0","creator":"Jellymon","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/99134483@N00/3330410116","source":"Flickr"},{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/c126b7d3-bf30-475a-9fda-6e70f14c9024/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/88/222038535_05fb767cf2.jpg","title":"Don't Believe The Hypebeast","license":"BY-NC-SA 2.0","creator":"coutorture","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/30381515@N00/222038535","source":"Flickr"},{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/f7dcfc56-5f11-4939-a747-ebc163ce8e6f/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/3059/3538067443_84d44f7707.jpg","title":"hypebeast-solebox-adidas-bianchi-bike-4","license":"BY-SA 2.0","creator":"adifansnet","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/35301442@N07/3538067443","source":"Flickr"},{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/71fa005d-3fc8-4dea-87a7-73ffbba2c835/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/2104/3538067401_92f462a2ce.jpg","title":"hypebeast-solebox-adidas-bianchi-bike-5","license":"BY-SA 2.0","creator":"adifansnet","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/35301442@N07/3538067401","source":"Flickr"}],"links":{"studies":[],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Wanna Be Powerlifter","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/wanna-be-powerlifter/229557","site":"T Nation · 1350 posts · 2017"},{"title":"Electoral Politics: A Losing Game","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/electoral-politics-a-losing-game/277629","site":"T Nation · 948 posts · 2022"},{"title":"Nike Free's?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/nike-frees/64102","site":"T Nation · 136 posts · 2006"},{"title":"What's Your Style?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/whats-your-style/81890","site":"T Nation · 107 posts · 2007"},{"title":"Your Favourite Casio Watch","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/your-favourite-casio-watch/176030","site":"T Nation · 59 posts · 2012"},{"title":"Would You Model?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/would-you-model/197932","site":"T Nation · 53 posts · 2014"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Hypebeast (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypebeast"},{"title":"Streetwear (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Streetwear"},{"title":"About Hypebeast","url":"https://www.hypebeast.com/about"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Style & presentation","chain":["Follow drops and collaborations","Acquire recognisable limited pieces","Current, branded streetwear look"],"effect":"direct","text":"Hypebeast culture gives a concrete clothing formula: sneakers, hoodies, tees and logo pieces from sought-after releases, assembled into a streetwear look that signals being up to date."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Hypebeast culture is a contemporary youth culture focused on clothing styles, in which followers seek limited, buzzworthy streetwear and logo-forward items [1]. It is part of the broader streetwear scene that grew out of New York hip-hop and West Coast surf and skate culture in the late 1970s and 1980s [2].","Brands use drops, very limited capsule collections promoted through social media, and artificial scarcity, which produced limited editions and resale markets for sneakers and clothing [2]. The word hypebeast arose in the mid-2000s as African-American Vernacular English for people buying streetwear mainly to follow trends and was initially derogatory; Kevin Ma then used it as the name of his fashion blog [2]. Hypebeast the company says it launched in 2005 and listed publicly in 2016, and its media and retail businesses cover fashion, footwear, art and design [3].","As a style approach, hypebeast dressing offers a way of looking current: recognisable pieces and sneakers, coordinated around current releases."],"infobox":[["Type","Fashion subculture / style approach"],["Origin","Mid-2000s slang; streetwear roots in 1970s-80s [2]"],["Key brands","Supreme, Stussy, A Bathing Ape [2]"],["Key mechanism","Limited drops, resale [2]"],["Media","Hypebeast (launched 2005) [3]"]],"sections":[{"h":"Origins and spread","paras":["Streetwear emerged from New York hip-hop in the late 1970s and early 1980s, then absorbed Los Angeles surf and skate culture; Shawn Stussy's 1980s printed T-shirts helped establish its focus on T-shirts and exclusivity [2]. Complex magazine named Supreme, Stussy and A Bathing Ape among top streetwear brands, and Supreme later made capsule collections with Louis Vuitton [2].","The hypebeast label appeared in the mid-2000s and its meaning varies by region, with some people now using it ironically or affectionately [2]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Practice","paras":["Followers watch release announcements, buy at retail or through resale, and wear pieces with visible branding. Online communities share outfit photos and release news. Lifting-oriented forums have also referenced the word jokingly for brand enthusiasts, for example a poster calling himself a hypebeast for a gym apparel brand [4]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Criticism","paras":["Critics describe resale of limited sneakers as prioritising financial gain and prestige over cultural or stylistic significance [2]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1980s","event":"Shawn Stussy's printed T-shirts help establish streetwear [2]."},{"year":"2005","event":"Hypebeast launches as a fashion blog and later a media company [3]."},{"year":"2016","event":"Hypebeast becomes publicly listed [3]."}],"refs":[{"title":"Hypebeast (disambiguation)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypebeast","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Streetwear","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Streetwear","source":"Wikipedia","year":2026,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"About Hypebeast","url":"https://www.hypebeast.com/about","source":"Hypebeast","year":2026,"type":"news"},{"title":"Wanna Be Powerlifter","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/wanna-be-powerlifter/229557","source":"T Nation forum","year":2017,"type":"forum"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Wanna Be Powerlifter","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/wanna-be-powerlifter/229557","site":"T Nation · 1350 posts · 2017"},{"title":"Electoral Politics: A Losing Game","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/electoral-politics-a-losing-game/277629","site":"T Nation · 948 posts · 2022"},{"title":"Nike Free's?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/nike-frees/64102","site":"T Nation · 136 posts · 2006"},{"title":"What's Your Style?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/whats-your-style/81890","site":"T Nation · 107 posts · 2007"},{"title":"Your Favourite Casio Watch","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/your-favourite-casio-watch/176030","site":"T Nation · 59 posts · 2012"},{"title":"Would You Model?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/would-you-model/197932","site":"T Nation · 53 posts · 2014"}]}